# scHopfield
#
# Written for this repository, not inherited. The single-repo file it replaces excluded by
# blanket extension (*.npz, *.png, *.csv, *.pdf) and then clawed individual files back with
# negations. That is what hid the figure inputs: a negation cannot reach into a directory
# git has already excluded, so files were invisible for reasons nobody had decided.
#
# The rule here is the other way round. Nothing under reproducibility/ is excluded by
# extension. Regenerable artifacts are named one by one, so anything new that lands beside
# a tracked input shows up in `git status` and gets a decision instead of disappearing.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- Environments
.env
.venv
.venv*/
env/
venv/
ENV/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.tox/
.nox/
.hypothesis/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# -------------------------------------------------------------- Editors and the OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
~$*
._*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- Docs
# Sphinx build output. docs/notebooks/ holds rendered copies of the tutorials, written by
# the build; the directory itself is tracked so the build has somewhere to put them.
docs/_build/
docs/api/generated/
docs/notebooks/*
!docs/notebooks/.gitkeep

# ------------------------------------------------------- Figure and report output
# Everything the figure scripts render. See reproducibility/paths.py.
reproducibility/figures/
reproducibility/output/

# ------------------------------------------------- Data roots that are not versioned
# The raw datasets, the base GRN scaffolds, and the per-dataset report tree. All three are
# located by environment variable and default to these paths; none is distributed here.
/data/
/reports/

# ------------------------------------------- Regenerated dyngen artifacts, named exactly
# Everything else under reproducibility/data/dyngen/ is tracked. adata.h5ad is rebuilt from
# the committed CSVs by reproducibility/dyngen/02_build_h5ad.py in about 15 s per backbone,
# progressions.csv is written by the R simulation and read by nothing, and install.log is a
# machine-specific build transcript. The provenance that matters is the seed and version in
# 01_simulate.R plus simulate.log, and both are tracked.
reproducibility/data/dyngen/*/adata.h5ad
reproducibility/data/dyngen/*/progressions.csv
reproducibility/data/dyngen/install.log

# --------------------------------------------------------------- Fitted checkpoints
# A fitted model is a large binary that goes stale against the method. Save your own with
# sch.tl.save_model; none is distributed, with one named exception below.
*.h5sch

# The exception, named rather than left to a blanket rule. The tutorials fit this checkpoint
# in docs/tutorials/01-getting-started.ipynb and the later tutorials load it, so a reader
# without a GPU never has to run the fit. It is 7.4 MB because save_model stores the model
# parameters and not the experiment, and it is regenerated byte for byte by re-running that
# first notebook, so it is not a black box. Regenerate it whenever the fit configuration
# changes, exactly as the figures are regenerated.
!docs/tutorials/pancreas_fitted.h5sch

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------- Scratch
scratch/
